course: dictionary
lesson: 3479
title: Truth and falsehood
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A falsehood is something that is not true. It is another word for a lie, and writers often use it in formal writing or old stories. «Put off falsehood and speak truthfully to your neighbour» tells you to stop telling lies and to be honest.
explain: Use the words around falsehood to work out its meaning. The sentence says to speak truthfully, which is the opposite of telling falsehoods. Truth is the opposite of falsehood, so a falsehood is the thing that is not true.
explain: Falsehood can also mean the state of being untrue. The phrase «truth and falsehood» means the difference between what is true and what is not. «"Alternative facts" means falsehoods, things that are not true» gives you the meaning straight away, after the word means.
explain: Always check by swapping your meaning into the sentence. Does "Alternative facts means lies, things that are not true" still make sense? It does, so your meaning is right.
fact: Falsehood means a lie, or something that is not true.
fact: The phrase «tell a falsehood» means to say something that is not true.
fact: «Truth and falsehood» means the difference between what is true and what is not true.
fact: «Spread falsehoods» means to pass false stories on to other people.
fact: Falsehood is a more formal word than lie, so you will often meet it in books, speeches and old stories.
exercise: «Put off falsehood and speak truthfully to your neighbour.» What does falsehood mean here? | A long walk to school | A loud noise | *A lie, something that is not true | A kind word said to a friend
exercise: «"Alternative facts" means falsehoods, things that are not true.» What are falsehoods? | Very big facts | Things that are always true | Facts that are very old | *Things that are not true
exercise: Which phrase means to pass false stories on to other people? | speak truthfully | tell the time | keep a secret | *spread falsehoods
test: Why might a writer choose the word falsehood instead of lie? | It means the same as truth | It is a word for a happy song | *It is a more formal word for a lie | It is only used for animals
test: In the phrase «truth and falsehood», what does falsehood mean? | *Whatever is not true | A type of food | A loud argument | Whatever is true
exam: Which word means the opposite of falsehood? | *truth | lie | rumour | joke
